cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use phylokit-mcp in your work, please cite it as below. IQ-TREE 3 is the
  inference engine this server drives, through piqtree, and both must be cited
  separately — see references.
title: phylokit-mcp
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for phylogenetic inference, driving
  IQ-TREE 3 through piqtree. It enforces one structural rule: a topology without
  support is not a result. Tree inference always runs a bootstrap and always
  returns per-clade support, with no flag to skip it. Threads are pinned before
  the engine is imported, because likelihood sums accumulate in a
  thread-dependent order and unpinned runs are not reproducible.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arnold
    given-names: Jaret
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4055-5238"
repository-code: "https://github.com/musharna/phylokit-mcp"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21713870
url: "https://pypi.org/project/phylokit-mcp/"
license: GPL-2.0-only
version: 0.6.0
date-released: "2026-09-26"
keywords:
  - phylogenetics
  - iqtree
  - bootstrap
  - maximum-likelihood
  - bioinformatics
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp
